  "The Houston Lyceum and Carnegie Library opened on March 2, 1904, at McKinney and Travis. The state marker says Carnegie offered $50,000 (Wikipedia's list says $65,000) and that the Martin and Moodie Company designed and built it; Wikipedia credits J. Riely Gordon. It was torn down to make way for the Julia Ideson Building, which replaced it in 1926.",
